#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""grip-claude-fleet -- which machine holds which Claude token, and making it so.

  grip-claude-fleet check [--json]         survey every machine. Passive: no call to
                                           the vendor, and nothing is written anywhere
  grip-claude-fleet identify [label ...]   one tiny live call per machine and label,
                                           made on that machine
  grip-claude-fleet converge               plan what would make every cell verified
  grip-claude-fleet converge --apply       do it: copy a token to each machine that
                                           lacks it, where the gates are open
  grip-claude-fleet strays                 tokens lying in shell files: where, by file
                                           and line number
  grip-claude-fleet strays --live          and whether the service still accepts each
  grip-claude-fleet strays --deep          also look in what each harness keeps (prompt
                                           history, session records, shell snapshots)
  grip-claude-fleet strays --remove --machine NAME
                                           delete the lines that carry a token, there
  grip-claude-fleet keychain [--live]      what the keychain items that hold a Claude
                                           token hold, by digest
  grip-claude-fleet keychain --set ITEM=LABEL
                                           put a stored token into one of those items
  grip-claude-fleet forget LABEL           remove a kept copy (such as laurie-old) from
                                           every machine where the service refuses it

Run it on the machine that holds the tokens. The machine list is yours and
holds host names, so it lives outside every repository:
``${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:-~/.config}/grip/claude-fleet.json``. Run any command
without one to be shown what it looks like.

A token is copied onto a machine only when the token canary passes there and
no token-shaped text is lying in its shell files. It travels on the
connection's standard input and is never printed.

Exit code: 0 everything is as it should be, 1 it is not, 2 the machine list is
missing or wrong.

How it works and what it does not cover: ``lib/claude_fleet.py``.
"""
from __future__ import annotations

import sys
from pathlib import Path

sys.path.insert(0, str(Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent / "lib"))

import claude_fleet  # noqa: E402

if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(claude_fleet.main())
